---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { B, money } from '../lib/shop';
import { edge, TTL_STATIC } from '../lib/cache';
const d = B.fulfilment.delivery[0];
const addr = (B.registered_address ?? []).join(', ');
edge(Astro.response, TTL_STATIC);
---

<Base
  title="Terms and conditions"
  description={`The terms on which ${B.legal_name} sells framed art prints.`}
>
  <div class="wrap page narrow">
    <h1>Terms and conditions</h1>
    <p class="meta" style="color:var(--ink-3);font-size:0.86rem">
      These terms apply to every order placed on this website.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      This shop is operated by <strong>{B.legal_name}</strong>, a company
      registered in England and Wales under company number
      {' '}{B.company_number}, registered office {addr}. Our VAT
      registration number is {B.vat_number}. You can reach us at
      {' '}<a href={`mailto:${B.email}`}>{B.email}</a> or {B.phone}.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What we sell</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Framed printed reproductions of digitally created artwork, made to
      order. They are not paintings, originals, limited editions or signed
      works. Sizes and frame options are stated on each product page, and
      the size given is the framed size.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Prices</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      All prices are in pounds sterling and <strong>include VAT</strong> at
      the UK standard rate. Delivery is
      {d.price === 0 ? ' free' : ` ${money(d.price)} per order`} and is shown
      before you pay. The price you see at checkout is the total you will be
      charged — there are no surcharges, handling fees or customs charges
      for UK delivery.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Your order</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Placing an order is an offer to buy. The contract forms when we email
      you to confirm. If we cannot fulfil an order — for example if a design
      has to be withdrawn — we will tell you and refund you in full. We
      reserve the right to decline an order, in which case you are not
      charged.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Payment</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Payment is taken at checkout by Stripe Payments UK Ltd. We do not see
      or store your card number. Your order is made once payment has
      cleared.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Delivery</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      We deliver to the United Kingdom only. Printing and framing take up to
      {' '}{B.fulfilment.dispatch_working_days} working days and delivery a
      further {d.min_days}–{d.max_days} working days. These are honest
      estimates, not guarantees; if an order is going to be materially late
      we will tell you. Risk passes to you on delivery.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Cancellation and returns</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      You may return anything within {B.returns.window_days} days of
      delivery for a full refund, for any reason. That is offered in
      addition to your statutory rights under the Consumer Contracts
      Regulations 2013 and the Consumer Rights Act 2015, and nothing in
      these terms restricts those rights. Full detail, including who pays
      return postage, is on the <a href="/returns">returns page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      The artwork, the photographs and this website belong to us. You are
      buying a physical print for private use. You are not buying the
      copyright, and the print may not be reproduced, resold as a digital
      file or used commercially without our written permission.
    </p>

    <h2>9. If we have got something wrong</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Tell us. We would much rather fix it than argue about it. Email
      {' '}<a href={`mailto:${B.email}`}>{B.email}</a> and we will reply
      within one working day. We do not limit our liability for death or
      personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud, or for anything else
      that cannot lawfully be limited.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Law</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales, and the
      courts of England and Wales have jurisdiction. If you live elsewhere
      in the UK you may bring proceedings in your own country.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
